    "Title": "SARS-CoV inhibition",
    "Description": "Estimates whether a compound inhibits the SARS-CoV-2 main protease, 3CLpro, by blocking its cleavage of peptide substrates, a target central to early repurposing efforts against COVID-19. The model applies the directed message-passing architecture that Stokes and colleagues established for antibiotic discovery, retrained here on coronavirus protease screening data. Activity against an isolated enzyme does not guarantee antiviral effect in cells, where permeability and stability also apply.",
